  <section class="summary" aria-labelledby="sum">
    <h2 id="sum">The 30 second version</h2>
    <div><span class="k">Problem</span><p>The things that actually break a budget don’t run on a monthly clock. In a normal year there are around eight of these, and a monthly view sees none of them until they land.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">Decision</span><p>So I flipped the model. Twelve plans across the next twelve months, and today’s number is what falls out of that plan.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">The one metric that matters</span><p>Bills that arrive already covered. If Twelve works, this share climbs every month.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">What I learned</span><p>You can’t assert AI. You have to show it working.</p></div>
  </section>

